body:
This is quite unfortunate, I had the impression that Tombi had much better groundwork (and the codebase seemed much more reasonable as well).

I have been using taplo since the beginning as it fits my needs but I cannot deny the fact that it has a lot of bugs and the code is unmaintainable as-is, since an all-around refactor/rewrite is more time consuming than anyone is willing to take on, it is destined to eventually die.

@ya7010 would you be open to some collaboration in order incorporate taplo's features and configuration into tombi so that we can sunset this project?

@tamasfe 
As many have mentioned here, Taplo is a fantastic project that provided me with many ideas when creating Tombi.

To accommodate Taplo users, Tombi will change its policy and accept formatter options.

@joshka @teohhanhui @ia0 Everyone else

I will create [a Project for the migration from Tombi to Taplo](https://github.com/orgs/tombi-toml/projects/6).
I may not be able to accept everything from Taplo, but please create any Issues deemed necessary for the migration within the Project.

@titaniumtraveler 
I wasn't familiar with GitHub boards 🙏 
I changed it to public.
